uinely out of scope, name it in excluded_source_handles\".\nI will review the routed sources for Ch5.\nP0311 (CAR-T focus) -> Might be excluded or used for analogy. Let's exclude if it doesn't discuss ICI in solid tumors significantly. The abstract says \"Targeting the gut microbiota to enhance... CAR-T...\". It mentions solid tumor efficacy data for CAR-T is disappointing. It might be less relevant for ICI intervention chapter. I will exclude it to keep focus.\nP0307 (Yeast-based for MSS CRC) -> Relevant for intervention.\nP0500 (Bariatric surgery) -> Relevant for diet intervention.\nMost others are reviews or ICI trials. I will keep them.\n\nWait, I need to check the `source_routing` provided in the input. It's a long list. I should not copy the whole list into the output. I only need to report `excluded_source_handles` if I decide to drop any.\nThe instruction says \"Use the complete source_routing ledger... Do not discard routed sources merely because they were not deep-read... When an individual source is genuinely out of scope, name it in excluded_source_handles\".\nSo I will list the handles of sources I decide NOT to use in the chapter text in `excluded_source_handles`.\nGiven the broad nature of reviews, most can contribute to background or context. I will be conservative and only exclude those clearly irrelevant (e.g. purely CAR-T, purely hematologic without solid tumor comparison).\nP0311: CAR-T focus. Exclude.\nP0303: Review, relevant.\nP0316: TCM review, relevant for intervention strategies.\nP0445: Affordable immunotherapy, relevant for context.\nI will check the `chapter_ids` in `source_routing`. If `Ch5_Interventions` is in the list, it's assigned. I should only exclude if I find it unusable during planning.\nI will exclude P0311 (CAR-T focus) and maybe P0445 (if it's too general on cost without microbiome specifics, but abstract says \"microbiome therapy... as low cost\", so keep).\nActually, to be safe and compliant with \"Do not silently drop\", I